# Claude Code — commit project knowledge (.claude/agent-memory/, CLAUDE.md,
# settings.json, .claude/skills/) but ignore per-developer state + secrets.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.credentials.json
.claude/.session*
.claude/projects/
.claude/todos/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/hooks/*.local.*
.gstack/

# Generated dogfood/workspace artifacts (keep the canonical files only).
# AWF writes per-workspace plan/conformance/validation files here at runtime
# (the awf-self profile's `plan_path: docs/awf-plans/{workspace_id}.md`); they
# are not part of the public source tree. The `**/` prefix de-anchors the rule
# so the folder is ignored at ANY depth: an agent that writes the plan from a
# subdir CWD (e.g. `apps/console/docs/awf-plans/`) is still covered (#620). We
# ignore the directory *contents* (trailing `/*`), not the directory itself, so
# the `README.md` re-inclusion below keeps working — git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.
**/docs/awf-plans/*
!docs/awf-plans/README.md
/TODO/
# `plans/` holds the Plan-and-Validate protocol's working docs (AGENTS.md): the
# generated `<TOPIC>_PLAN.md` / `<TOPIC>_VALIDATION.md` are LOCAL working
# artifacts and are NOT committed (they had accumulated to 600+ tracked files,
# one PLAN+VALIDATION pair per task incl. every review-comment fix). Mirror the
# awf-plans rule above: ignore the directory *contents*, keep the protocol
# definition and this folder's README tracked. Agents must NOT `git add -f` the
# generated docs — keep the planning discipline, not the files.
/plans/*
!/plans/README.md
!/plans/PLAN_EXECUTION_PROTOCOL.md
